  "Question": "If \\[a \\otimes b = \\dfrac{a + b}{a - b},\\] then \\[(6 \\otimes 4) \\otimes 3 =\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(13\\)",
    "C": "\\(15\\)",
    "D": "\\(30\\)",
    "E": "\\(72\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The parentheses tell us to calculate \\(6\\otimes4\\) first. Substitute the two inputs into the given rule:\n\\[\n6\\otimes4=\\frac{6+4}{6-4}=\\frac{10}{2}=5.\n\\]\nNow use \\(5\\) as the first input and \\(3\\) as the second:\n\\[\n(6\\otimes4)\\otimes3=5\\otimes3\n=\\frac{5+3}{5-3}=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n\\]\nBoth denominators are \\(2\\), so both operations are defined. The value is \\(4\\), choice A.",
